From a3229a005430d96acff01bc8280d7e414c2909cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:20:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] CA-430073: VM.create bypasses per-key RBAC on
 other_config and platform protected keys

This defeats the _R_POOL_ADMIN per-key gates that XSA-489 added for
VM.other_config:pci and VM.platform:hvm_serial.

Additionally, there are other paths that may bypass the gate: VM clone
and import. Note that the API calls are forwarded to supporter hosts
with session created by pool secret. It needs to be recovered to the
original session for RBAC check.

VM.create only needs the VM admin role, but it takes a whole VM record,
including fields whose setters need a higher role. Two of them are
checked as well:

  - ha_restart_priority: a VM with "restart" is protected by HA and takes
    resources from the pool's point of view.
  - appliance: is managed from pool's point of view as well.

There are other VM fields which currently require higher role. But one
of them, ha_always_run, is deprecated. Others seem not necessary to be
managed by higher role, or from the pool's point of view.

Includes unit tests for the per-key RBAC check on maps of VM, and for
the RBAC check on protected fields of VM.

This is CVE-2026-102706, part of XSA-530.

Signed-off-by: Ming Lu <ming.lu@citrix.com>
Reviewed-by: Andrii Sultanov <andriy.sultanov@vates.tech>
